# The project clones, which are SEPARATE git repositories that happen to sit
# inside this working tree. Each has its own .git and its own remote; this repo
# is the registry (PROJECTS.md) and the shared guard, not their parent.
#
# Without this, every session in one of them ends with the stop hook reporting
# untracked files and asking for a commit that must never happen: committing a
# nested clone either vendors a whole second repository into this one or writes
# a gitlink pointing at a commit this repo cannot fetch. Neither is recoverable
# by the person who runs it by accident, and the warning fired on two
# consecutive days before this line existed.
df-correspondence/
